WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.108
The lasting takeaway is that fine-tuning no longer
strictly requires backpropagation.

00:00:05.188 --> 00:00:09.869
With MeZO, you can adapt very large language models
using only forward passes,

00:00:09.949 --> 00:00:11.822
at the memory cost of inference,

00:00:11.902 --> 00:00:16.216
and still match the quality of gradient-based
fine-tuning on many tasks.

00:00:16.296 --> 00:00:21.587
This overturns the classical worry that
zeroth-order methods must scale badly with model

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:24.822
size: when you start from a strong pre-trained model,

00:00:24.902 --> 00:00:30.010
convergence is governed by the effective local
structure of the loss landscape rather

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:32.207
than the sheer number of parameters,

00:00:32.287 --> 00:00:35.320
which is why MeZO works at billion-parameter scale.
